This directory supports translation from HOL4 to ACL2 -- more
specifically, from HOL4 to ACL2(zfc), the integration of set theory
with ACL2 supported by community books directory projects/set-theory/.
The translation process actually consists of two parts:  a
translator from HOL4 to defhol forms, and a translator from defhol
forms to ACL2(zfc).  For the first of these, see:

https://github.com/HOL-Theorem-Prover/HOL/blob/master/examples/acl2/hol-to-acl2/

The work here concerns the second part of the translation process:
from defhol forms to ACL2(zfc).

Subdirectory v1/ contains an initial version, as described in the
following paper (to appear).

  Kaufmann, M., Slind, K.: Translating HOL to ACL2 with set theory.
  In: Nipkow, T., Passmore, G., Sultana, N. (eds.) Logic, Computation
  and Proof, vol. 16870.  Springer Nature Switzerland (2026)

A version of that paper may be made publicly available in late 2027
according to the terms of the license with Springer.

This work in progress continues in subdirectory v2/, which among other
improvements contains support for HOL4 datatype definitions.

Examples may be found in the examples/ subdirectory of each of those
subdirectories, as discussed in examples/README.txt.

Soundness considerations are addressed in soundness/README.txt.
